#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:1
msgid "From Python CuTeDSL to cute-rs"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:3
msgid ""
"If you have used NVIDIA's Python **CuTeDSL**, the concepts in cute-rs will "
"feel immediately familiar: layouts, composed swizzles, `zipped_divide`, TMA "
"copy atoms, and tiled MMA. Both compile down to the **exact same CUTLASS "
"`cute` and `cute_nvgpu` MLIR operations**."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:5
msgid ""
"The key difference is **where the static configuration lives** and **when "
"the IR is constructed**:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:11
msgid ""
"Python CuTeDSL traces Python objects wrapping live MLIR values at runtime; "
"Rust cute-rs encodes layouts, swizzles, and MMA plans in Rust types and "
"translates them ahead of time."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:16
msgid "Why the Kernel Signatures Look Different"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:18
msgid ""
"In Python **CuTeDSL**, `@cute.jit` traces a Python function at runtime to "
"build an MLIR module. Because Python objects like `cute.Tensor`, "
"`cute.CopyAtom`, `cute.TiledMma`, and `cute.ComposedLayout` directly wrap "
"MLIR values, the host script constructs all of them and passes them as "
"parameters into `@cute.kernel`:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:20
msgid ""
"# Python CuTeDSL: 18 parameters wrapping MLIR types during @cute.jit "
"tracing\n"
"@cute.kernel\n"
"def kernel(\n"
"    self,\n"
"    tma_atom_a: cute.CopyAtom,              mA_mkl: cute.Tensor,\n"
"    tma_atom_b: cute.CopyAtom,              mB_nkl: cute.Tensor,\n"
"    tma_atom_sfa: cute.CopyAtom,            mSFA_mkl: cute.Tensor,\n"
"    tma_atom_sfb: cute.CopyAtom,            mSFB_nkl: cute.Tensor,\n"
"    tma_atom_c: cute.CopyAtom,              mC_mnl: cute.Tensor,\n"
"    tiled_mma: cute.TiledMma,               cta_layout_mnk: cute.Layout,\n"
"    a_smem_layout: cute.ComposedLayout,     b_smem_layout: "
"cute.ComposedLayout,\n"
"    sfa_smem_layout: cute.Layout,           sfb_smem_layout: cute.Layout,\n"
"    epi_smem_layout: cute.ComposedLayout,   tile_sched_params: "
"PersistentTileSchedulerParams,\n"
"): ...\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:37
msgid ""
"In Rust **cute-rs**, there is no runtime tracer: rustc compiles the kernel "
"ahead of time. Nothing is hidden:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:38
msgid ""
"**Kernel parameters carry only the hardware launch ABI** (for example, 128-"
"byte hardware TMA descriptors passed by value via `#[grid_constant]`, device "
"pointers, and scalar dimensions)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:39
msgid ""
"**Layouts, swizzles, operand roles, and MMA configurations live in Rust "
"types** (`ASmem`, `Sm100TiledMma<...>`, `MainloopPipeline`) with zero "
"runtime byte overhead."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:41
msgid ""
"// Rust cute-rs: static configuration lives in types; arguments carry only "
"runtime TMA descriptors\n"
"type ASmem = ComposedLayout<Swizzle<3, 3, 3>, 0, RowMajor<128, 64>>;\n"
"type B0Smem = ComposedLayout<Swizzle<3, 3, 3>, 0, RowMajor<96, 64>>;\n"
"type B1Smem = ComposedLayout<Swizzle<3, 3, 3>, 0, RowMajor<80, 64>>;\n"
"type CSmem = ComposedLayout<Swizzle<2, 3, 3>, 0, RowMajor<128, 32>>;\n"
"type TiledMma = Sm100TiledMma<ASmem, B0Smem, B1Smem, 192, 160>;\n"
"type MainloopPipeline = PipelineTmaUmma<5, 77_824>;\n"
"\n"
"#[kernel]\n"
"pub fn fp16_gemm_256x352(\n"
"    #[grid_constant] a: &TensorMap<f16, ASmem>,\n"
"    #[grid_constant] b0: &TensorMap<f16, B0Smem>,\n"
"    #[grid_constant] b1: &TensorMap<f16, B1Smem>,\n"
"    #[grid_constant] c: &TensorMap<f16, CSmem>,\n"
"    bias: *const f16, m: u64, n: u64, k: u64, has_bias: u64,\n"
") { ... }\n"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:62
msgid "How mir-importer Translates Rust Types to CuTe IR"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:64
msgid ""
"When mir-importer translates a cute-rs call, it matches the callee's "
"canonical rustc `DefId`, structurally walks its monomorphized generic type "
"arguments (`static_config.rs`), runs cute-layout static validation proofs, "
"and emits a dialect-cute operation combining those static attributes with "
"the call's runtime SSA operands:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:70
msgid ""
"Compile-time Rust types supply the static IR attributes (shape, stride, "
"swizzle, operand role, MMA partitions), while kernel values supply the "
"runtime SSA operands."
msgstr ""

