#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:99
msgid "Where cute-rs Deviates, and Why"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:101
msgid ""
"The names follow CuTeDSL 4.7. Where the Rust form differs on purpose, the "
"difference and its reason are listed here, so a CuTeDSL author is not "
"surprised."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid "CuTeDSL 4.7"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid "Why"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid "**Constructors and plans**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`make_layout`, `make_tensor`, `make_tiled_mma` and `make_tiled_copy` build "
"objects while tracing"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`new` and `from_*` constructors; a compile-time plan is a type or a const "
"generic (`RowMajor<128, 64>`, `TiledCopy<Atom, ThreadLayout, ValueLayout, "
"TileLayout>`, `zipped_divide::<8>()`)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"the compiler reads the plan from the generic arguments, so there is nothing "
"for a `make_*` call to build"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`producer_acquire` folds the arrive-expect into the wait, under "
"`is_leader_cta` in `PipelineTmaUmma`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`producer_acquire` waits; the elected lane calls `producer_expect_tx`, or "
"`producer_expect_tx_cursor` on `TwoCtaRing`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"electing the lane is a convergence obligation the compiler does not prove, "
"so it stays visible in kernel code; the pipeline value stores pointers only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid "**Scheduler**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`WorkTileInfo.is_valid_tile`; `get_grid_shape(params, max_active_clusters)` "
"returns `(m, n, persistent_clusters)`; "
"`advance_to_next_work(advance_count=1)`; `tile_idx` is a `Coord`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`has_work()` on the scheduler; `get_grid_shape(sm_count, active_ctas_per_sm) "
"-> Option<u32>`; `advance_to_next_work()`; `tile_idx() -> (m, n, l)` with "
"`linear_idx()` beside it"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"the grid is one dimensional and has no params object; the bounds check stays "
"outside the coordinate arithmetic; the step is always one grid of blocks; "
"the coordinate is a Rust tuple"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid "`PipelineState.index` is an `Int32`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid "`PipelineState::index() -> usize`; `RingCursor::index() -> u32`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"a `usize` scales a shared-buffer offset directly; the SM100 attention ring "
"keeps the `u32` its barriers take"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid "**TMA names**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`make_tiled_tma_atom` returns the atom and a TMA tensor; one `cute.copy` "
"loads and stores"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`TensorMap` is the one descriptor type; `create_tensor_map_tiled` is the one "
"host encoder, with the rank-three SM100 form in `cute_rs::attention::sm100`; "
"`TmaCopy::load` and `TmaCopy::store` stay two methods; `size_in_bytes::<T, "
"SmemL>()` is `cute.size_in_bytes`, a cosize, so a padded row stride counts "
"and a swizzle does not"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"the descriptor is CUDA's `CUtensorMap` typed by element and shared layout; "
"load takes a barrier and a CTA rank and store takes neither, so one "
"signature cannot serve both"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid "**Clusters**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`cute.arch.cluster_dim()` is the number of clusters in the grid; "
"`cute.arch.block_in_cluster_dim()` is CTAs per cluster"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid "the same two names with the same meanings"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"the compiler's own `cluster_dim` vocabulary (the `#[cluster_launch]` "
"attribute, the `cluster_dim` field of `cuda_launch!` and the `cluster_dim_x/"
"y/z` NVVM annotations) means CTAs per cluster; in a kernel, `cluster_dim()` "
"reads as the DSL does and `block_in_cluster_dim()` is the launch value"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid "**Named barriers**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`pipeline.NamedBarrier(barrier_id, num_threads)` with `arrive_and_wait()`, "
"its alias `sync()`, `arrive()`, `wait()` and the unaligned forms"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`NamedBarrier::<ID, THREADS>::sync()` only; `cute_rs::arch::barrier(id, n)` "
"and `barrier_arrive(id, n)` are the `cute.arch` free functions"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"both values are const generics, so the id and the thread count (a multiple "
"of 32, at most 1024) are checked at compile time; the split arrive and wait "
"methods are not bound on the type"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid "**Sync-restricted fence**"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`fence_sync_restrict(order)` in the experimental primitives layer, `order` a "
"`MemOrder` string enum"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`cute_rs::arch::fence_sync_restrict::<Acquire>()`, the order a sealed marker "
"type; acquire only"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"the instruction is chosen when the kernel compiles; the release form waits "
"for its intrinsic to be bound"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`make_tiled_copy`, `get_slice`, `partition_S`, `partition_D`, `cute.copy`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`TiledCopy`, `get_slice` and `ThrCopy::copy` exist, but no kernel can reach "
"them yet"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`GlobalCopyTensor` has no public constructor: `from_carrier` is `pub(crate)` "
"and the only public producers are the block-scaled tensors' "
"`values_for_copy` and `scale_words_for_copy`; the importer's "
"`shared_tensor_overlay` hook accepts only the block-scaled roles `Mkl` and "
"`Nkl`; the verifier rejects a role-typed shared carrier as a `copy_g2s` "
"destination. The kernels that need a block-wide copy call `copy_g2s` directly"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`/` on integer vectors converts both sides to f32 and divides; `//` floors; "
"`-a` is `0 - a`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"`/` on integer lanes truncates toward zero; unary `-` negates each lane, so "
"a `+0.0` lane becomes `-0.0`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:66
msgid ""
"the operators are Rust's own: floating-point division matches the DSL, "
"integer division and the sign of a negated zero differ"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../cute/cutedsl-comparison.md:116
msgid ""
"ctm-rs keeps PTX instruction names "
"(`cp_async_bulk_tensor_shared_cta_global`, `mbarrier_arrive_expect_tx`, "
"`fence_sync_restrict_acquire`); the `cute.arch` concept names live in "
"`cute_rs::arch` as forwarders over them. Dialect op, type and attribute "
"names are compiler-internal and are not part of this surface."
msgstr ""
